Article 46

To anticipate and prevent acts of violence against Women from occurring, the Regional Government shall undertake the following efforts:
a. b. f. providing various proper public facilities for Women in public spaces;

developing an integrated information system database on acts of violence against Women,;

strengthening the competence of apparatus handling violence against Women;

creating various modules and guidelines on the prevention and handling of acts of violence against Women,;

conducting various trainings and guidance for social workers engaged in organizations/institutions handling violence against Women,;

inviting the community to play an active role in recovery and reintegration;

strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in the field of Women's empowerment; conducting various socializations regarding the prevention and anticipation of acts of violence against Women to various community components in the Region; and optimizing the role of religious institutions, customary institutions, culture, as well as exploring local wisdom in order to prevent and minimize violence against Women both occurring at home or outside the home.

Article 44

The Regional Government in its efforts to protect Women as referred to in Article 42 is responsible for carrying out the following matters:
a. planning, making, establishing and organizing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women;

strengthening and developing institutions providing Women's protection services,;

conducting various preventive efforts early on so that violence against Women does not occur or can be minimized;

massively and continuously making various efforts to prevent acts of violence against Women in all fields of life;

massively and continuously preventing the occurrence of TPPO; and
f. continuously striving to provide protection for Women workers.

Article 45

In order for the efforts to protect Women as referred to in Article 44 to be carried out properly, the Regional Government shall coordinate, cooperate and partner with the following parties:
a. the central government through vertical agencies in the Region;

City/city governments in Riau province;

social and religious institutions;

customary institutions;

non-governmental organizations;
f. universities; and media.

